    <string name="privacy_text">Redes has no ads or analytics. It reads what Android says about your connection, your SIMs (carrier, network type and signal) and the Wi‑Fi networks nearby; the location or nearby devices permissions only serve to see network names: it never reads or keeps where you are. The speed test downloads and uploads filler data with Cloudflare\'s public server (speed.cloudflare.com); nothing of yours is sent. Latency is measured to your network\'s router and to that same Cloudflare server. «Discover» only asks the addresses of your local network and listens to Bluetooth adverts nearby while it is open; those lists are never kept and never leave the phone. Tests and access point changes are kept only on this phone, out of cloud backups. Only if you turn on MCP mode, the AI you connect with a token can see your connection, signal, latency and tests (never other devices\' hardware addresses) and, with a read-and-write token, start a speed or latency test, through the relay.</string>
